    "type": "question",
    "label": "7",
    "prompt": "Find the area enclosed by the curve $y=\\sqrt{3x-5}$, the $y$-axis and the lines $y=2$ and $y=3$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\dfrac{34}{9}\\text{ units}^2$",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}y^2&=3x-5\\\\x&=\\frac{y^2+5}{3}\\end{aligned}$$\n$$\\begin{aligned}A&=\\int_2^3\\frac{y^2+5}{3}\\,dy\\\\A&=\\frac13\\left[\\frac{y^3}{3}+5y\\right]_2^3\\\\A&=\\frac13\\left[(9+15)-\\left(\\frac83+10\\right)\\right]\\\\A&=\\frac{34}{9}\\\\A&=3\\frac79\\text{ units}^2\\end{aligned}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
